## Context
Parent tracker 0999 spans runtime registration and memory-helper portability.
PR 1091 owns registration, launch protection, mechanical consumers and safe
operator documentation. The extracted legacy memory-helper handoff 1002 was
later closed WONTDO; 0988 retains the separate memory ownership/synchronization
decision for v8.

## Relevant files
adapters/lifecycle.py, adapters/projections.json, scripts/validate-projections.py,
scripts/gen-claude-code-adapter-hooks.py, shell entry points, tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py,
README.md, docs/idh-install-strategy.md, docs/adapter-operations.md, adapters/README.md.

## Test
Install with independent runtime profiles in disposable HOME at ~/.agents
and an arbitrary space-containing checkout. Preserve user content, move the
checkout and re-register through installed launchers. Start from the exact
shipped legacy Codex guard and retain an unrelated hook: one portable guard
must replace the predecessor and installation must be idempotent. The author
removed migration-specific tests/ratchets; predecessor repair is verified
by a one-off behavioral probe, not a persistent old-layout test corpus.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Fresh and arbitrary-path installation and explicit relocation/re-registration pass without a ~/.idh pointer or whole-profile repository alias.
- [ ] Runtime settings, unrelated hooks, skills, rules and extensions are preserved; modified/foreign registered links are not overwritten.
- [ ] Exact shipped Claude and Codex hook predecessors migrate once, preserving unrelated hooks and semantics.
- [ ] Current registration docs match the installer, explain receipt-owned relocation and do not delete merged user configuration during removal or recovery.
- [ ] Full make check and make lint pass; Claude, Codex and Pi registration/guard smoke evidence is recorded with its limitations.

This child does not certify dream/provenance portability, memory ownership,
store reconciliation, native plugin parity or opt-in shell integration.
Parent 0999 closed after integration review in PR #1104. The memory v8 pilot
0920 is downstream work, not an acceptance prerequisite for this registration
child.
